---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL } from "../lib/site";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy · Up.computer" description="What the Up.computer app and website collect.">
  <LegalPage
    title="Privacy Policy"
    description="What the Up.computer app and this website collect, and what they don’t."
    effectiveDate="October 3, 2026"
  >
    <h2>Who operates Up.computer</h2>
    <p>
      Up.computer is operated by Kirill Gurianov. Privacy and data requests can be sent to{" "}
      <a href="mailto:support@up.computer">support@up.computer</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Your data stays on your computer</h2>
    <p>
      Projects, chats, and settings are stored on your computer. When you ask an agent to work, the
      content it needs goes to the provider you chose, such as Claude Code or Codex, under that
      provider’s own terms. Websites and apps an agent opens through the browser or computer use see
      what it sends them.
    </p>

    <h2>App telemetry</h2>
    <p>
      The app sends usage events to PostHog: app version, operating system, processor architecture,
      provider, model, interaction and access mode, counts, durations, and error categories. Events
      never include prompts, responses, file contents, file paths, or credentials. They are tied to a
      pseudonymous ID: a SHA-256 hash of your local Codex or Claude Code account ID if there is one,
      otherwise of a random ID the app creates. Set <code>UPCOMPUTER_TELEMETRY_ENABLED=false</code>
      to turn it off. The code is{" "}
      <a href={`${GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL}/tree/main/apps/server/src/telemetry`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">open source</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Website</h2>
    <p>
      This website counts page views, Core Web Vitals, and clicks on download, GitHub, and changelog
      links with PostHog, without cookies, persistent identifiers, or session replay. It respects Do
      Not Track and Global Privacy Control. Hosting logs may include IP address, user agent, time,
      and requested path for security and reliability.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention and your choices</h2>
    <p>
      Local data stays until you delete it. Telemetry is kept only as long as it helps operate and
      improve the app. Data held by providers follows their policies. Send access or deletion
      requests to the contact above.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>Updates will be published on this page with a new effective date.</p>
  </LegalPage>
</Layout>
